[Rotproof](https://github.com/secta113/rotproof) keeps the layers and the records in `docs/`. It is pinned in
`requirements-dev.txt`, and CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs `rotproof check`.

```sh
python -m venv venv
./venv/Scripts/python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt   # on Linux: ./venv/bin/python
./venv/Scripts/rotproof check                                  # on Linux: ./venv/bin/rotproof
```

Start your agent with the venv active: its stop hook runs `rotproof stop-hook`, which has to be on the `PATH`, and
runs the first one there. When it is not there, or is another version than the project's, the agent's session says so.
